      subshell openings that do NOT reset : 11

  THE STATEMENT

      a resets ONLY at a subshell opening or an aufbau exception —
      never in the middle of a subshell's filling. so every subshell
      is filled at CONSTANT a, and its occupancy slope is a property
      of that subshell alone.

      the slopes are not comparable because the index says so, and the
      reset mechanism is WHY: each subshell is its own segment.
